15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers;
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence;
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning the System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;
19. Regional Regulation of Bali Province Number 6 of 2014 concerning Child Protection (Regional Gazette of Bali Province Year 2014 Number 6, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Bali Province Number 6 Year 2014);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BULELENG REGENCY and

Article 9
(1) Regional Governments are obligated to formulate Prevention programs or activities as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) in the Regional Work Plan and Regional Strategic Plan;
(2) Programs or activities as referred to in paragraph (1) are to support the realization of the Regional Long-Term Development Plan and Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.

Article 14
(1) Regional Government conducts cooperation and coordination in order to ensure the implementation of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
(2) Cooperation and coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 10
(1) Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment shall implement prevention as referred to in Article 8;
